Subject: macos: mach_wait_until NtDelayExecution, QoS/avrt priority mapping, LatencyCritical, and batched kqueue

1. dlls/ntdll/unix/sync.c: Use mach_wait_until() for short non-alertable
   NtDelayExecution() sleeps (<=30s) on macOS instead of select() + spurious
   NtYieldExecution(), eliminating macOS timer-coalescing jitter on Sleep(1..16).
2. dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c & dlls/avrt/main.c: Map ThreadBasePriority to
   macOS pthread_set_qos_class_self_np() (P-core USER_INTERACTIVE for high/audio
   threads, E-core UTILITY/BACKGROUND for low-priority workers) and implement
   avrt.dll MMCSS priority elevation/restoration on top of SetThreadPriority()
   using a crash-safe opaque handle table.
3. dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m: Add NSActivityLatencyCritical when App Nap is
   disabled so macOS disables timer coalescing for active Wine processes.
4. server/fd.c: Batch steady-state kqueue EV_ADD/EV_ENABLE/EV_DISABLE changes
   into main_loop_epoll()'s kevent() call and emit delta-only filter updates,
   while flushing synchronously before EV_DELETE to stay fd-reuse safe.

